  "lineage": "1980s-and-onward American-Jewish jazz-fusion style integrating klezmer modal-and-melodic vocabulary with jazz-improvisational practice. Don Byron's Plays the Music of Mickey Katz (1993) and the Klezmatics 1980s-onward recordings constitute the canonical type-specimens; the parallel Frank London-led ensembles and David Krakauer's solo work extended the genre. Distinguished from broader klezmer revival by jazz-fusion's explicit jazz-improvisation-and-harmonic emphasis.",
  "recipe": "classic North American mid-1980s klezmer-jazz fusion, improv On Frame, klezmer improv branch, Jewish ritual devotional hasidic niggun sephardi bakkashot. thick, breath veiled tone, straight onset, interlocked note trading. ebonite hard rubber klezmer tradition continuous-airflow legato clarinet, alto nickel silver bright projecting selmer mark vi canonical 1954 1974 jazz paris continuous-airflow saxophone, cold pressed wurzen felt oversize maple tension resonator European spruce grand piano, growly gut upright bass, fiberskyn synthetic calf brushes-and-sticks drum kit, klezmer ensemble. nuyorican fania canon 1968-1977 mid tier fania la tierra studios ny. large-diaphragm condenser, Neve 1073 inductor pre, SSL inline console, dbx 160 VCA, SSL surgical EQ. Studer 30ips tape plate reverb digital delay.",
